analysis:
The PR changes only docs/provider/cli-reference.md. The changed hunk (head lines ~1968-1971, outside the supplied excerpts) updates the runtime constants table. It moves the coordinator reconnect backoff to a new CoordinatorReconnectPolicy and adds a 60s stable-session reset counted from the `register` frame. It also adds a random 0-1s reconnect delay after close code 1012. The ping/pong constants are unchanged, so this is a documentation edit with no executable or enforcement change.

The supplied units cover the earlier part of the file (lines 1-804), which is unchanged context. Its security statements agree with the canonical threat model:
- logout revokes only with HTTP 204, and offline logout is not remote invalidation (A-008);
- the hold socket, App Attest guidance and the macOS 27 upgrade notice grant no serving authorization (TB-011, T-052);
- the cache section keeps the encrypted SSD cache and its limits as in T-041, including the 30-minute TTL and DARKBLOOM_PREFIX_CACHE=0 opt-out.

I did not verify the new reconnect policy source (CoordinatorReconnectPolicy.swift). It is not supplied here and is outside the changed documentation. Possible integration questions are whether the 0-1s jitter after close 1012 could produce reconnect storms against the coordinator, and whether resetting backoff after 60s allows a stuck register loop. These are availability and operational concerns, and the evidence is insufficient to call them a regression. No threat-model assumption is invalidated by this documentation change.
